# t10-config-misc: integration fragment

## scripts/collect-client-inputs.mjs, OVERRIDE_ARGS (the clients-accepted corpus; lead regenerates the fixture)

Anchor: the line `  setRoute: [{ provider: 'p', model: 'm' }],` of the session-action sample arguments.

Replace it with what the remote chat really sends on a model pick (apps/desktop/src/renderer/remote-protocol-chat.ts
`setModelRoute`: `{ ...selection, applyToCurrentSession: true, keepMainModel: Boolean(sessionId) }`):

  setRoute: [{ provider: 'p', model: 'm', applyToCurrentSession: true, keepMainModel: true }],

and regenerate native/core/crates/mixdog-app-protocol/src/boundary/validate/fixtures/clients-accepted.json. The row
`session action setRoute` then carries the two options inside `params.route`; with this task's change of
boundary/validate/model.rs (`route_write`) the corpus tests accept it (`validate_model_clients_accepted_rows_pass`,
mixdog-app-server `clients_accepted_corpus_passes`). Before the change the validator refused that row with
"model selection contains an unsupported field.", which is what every remote model pick got.

No protocol method, table row or Cargo dependency is added by this task: nothing for methods.rs, params.rs,
inventory.rs, Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock or the workspace-hack.
